From: openRuyi Project Contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Report dynamic analyzer messages without Reportf

Go vet rejects passing a runtime string as the format argument to Reportf.
The analyzer message has no formatting arguments, so use the diagnostic API
while preserving the exact message and source range.

---
 noinlineerr.go | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/noinlineerr.go b/noinlineerr.go
--- a/noinlineerr.go
+++ b/noinlineerr.go
@@ -76,5 +76,9 @@ func inlineErrorInspector(pass *analysis.Pass) func(n ast.Node) {
 			// so don't do anything beside simple error message
 			if len(assignStmt.Lhs) != 1 || (assignStmt.Tok == token.DEFINE && shadowVarsExists(ident.Name, pass.TypesInfo.Scopes[ifStmt])) {
-				pass.Reportf(ident.Pos(), errMessage(assignStmt.Tok))
+				pass.Report(analysis.Diagnostic{
+					Pos:     ident.Pos(),
+					End:     ident.End(),
+					Message: errMessage(assignStmt.Tok),
+				})
 				return
 			}
